  "summary_en": "Japan's National Police Agency sets criteria for prefectural police to grant road use permits under the Road Traffic Act for public-road automated driving field tests, covering remote-type systems and special-device vehicles. It specifies vehicle, operator, communication, recording and safety requirements, permit conditions, and guidance.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Field tests are treated as special road use requiring a Road Traffic Act Art. 77 permit with individually tailored conditions.",
   "The monitoring/operator remains the legal driver with safe-driving duties; one operator per running vehicle.",
   "Vehicles must pass an on-road autonomous driving check by police and comply with safety standards.",
   "Remote systems require communication-loss safe stop, speed limited to stopping distance, and data/communication log recording.",
   "Permits last up to six months; incidents must be reported; operators should secure insurance and cybersecurity."
